In terms of code, you might want to implement this logic within a method that returns the longest substring. Here's a simple template:

```java
public String longestSubstringWithoutRepeatingChars(String s) {
    int start = 0;
    int maxLength = 0;
    HashSet<Character> set = new HashSet<>();
    for (int end = 0; end < s.length(); end++) {
        // Add the current character to the set
        set.add(s.charAt(end));

        // If a duplicate is found, remove characters from the start pointer
        while (set.contains(s.charAt(end))) {
            set.remove(s.charAt(start));
            start++;
        }

        // Update the maximum length if necessary
        if (end - start + 1 > maxLength) {
            maxLength = end - start + 1;
        }
    }

    return s.substring(start, start + maxLength);
}
```

